---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const baseURL = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/');
---
<BaseLayout title="Marcelo Ellwanger | Software & Systems Developer" description="Software and systems developer building practical tools across Windows diagnostics, local AI, automation, computer vision and evidence-driven data systems.">
  <section class="hero identity-hero wrap">
    <div class="identity-grid">
      <div class="identity-main">
        <div class="identity-kicker mono"><span class="identity-dot"></span><span>MARCELO ELLWANGER</span><span class="identity-kicker-muted">SOFTWARE · SYSTEMS · AI</span></div>
        <h1 class="identity-name">Software &amp;<br />systems developer.</h1>
        <div class="identity-statement">
          <p class="identity-role">I turn real-world friction into software that earns trust.</p>
          <p class="hero-copy">A hands-on builder working across local AI, Windows diagnostics, automation, computer vision and data. My projects begin with something I genuinely want to understand, fix or make easier.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button primary" href="#work">Explore selected work ↓</a>
          <a class="button" href="/about/">About me ↗</a>
          <a class="button" href="/resume/software/">Software / QA Résumé ↗</a>
        </div>
        <div class="identity-foot mono"><span>BASED IN JAPAN</span><i></i><span>REMOTE / GLOBAL</span><i></i><span>BUILDING IN PUBLIC</span></div>
      </div>

      <section class="project-carousel" role="region" aria-roledescription="carousel" aria-label="Featured projects" data-carousel>
        <div class="project-carousel-window">
          <a class="project-carousel-slide is-active" href="/projects/crashscope/" data-slide aria-hidden="false">
            <div class="carousel-slide-copy"><div class="project-top"><span class="eyebrow">01 · Windows diagnostics</span><span class="project-state">1.3 IN DEVELOPMENT · 1.2.0 RELEASED</span></div><h2>CrashScope</h2><p>Local-first Windows crash diagnostics with persistent incidents, Event Log + WER evidence and privacy-safe support bundles.</p><span class="carousel-link">Open case study ↗</span></div>
            <div class="carousel-visual-column"><div class="carousel-visual carousel-console" aria-hidden="true"><div class="priority-visual-head mono"><span>CURRENT / 1.3</span><b>DEVELOPMENT</b></div><div class="carousel-signal"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><div class="diagnostic-readout mono"><span>EVENT LOG</span><b>LINKED</b><span>WER</span><b>LINKED</b><span>TESTS</span><b>266/266</b></div><div class="diagnostic-foot mono"><span>LOCAL-FIRST</span><span>ROOT CAUSE: NOT ASSUMED</span></div></div></div>
          </a>
          <a class="project-carousel-slide" href="/projects/easyflix/" data-slide aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="carousel-slide-copy"><div class="project-top"><span class="eyebrow">02 · Windows local media</span><span class="project-state active">1.4.0 RELEASED</span></div><h2>EasyFlix</h2><p>A polished local-first media library built around real files, removable drives, watch-state continuity and a streaming-style WPF interface.</p><span class="carousel-link">Open case study ↗</span></div>
            <div class="carousel-visual-column"><figure class="carousel-visual carousel-shot easyflix-carousel-shot" style="--easyflix-backdrop:url('/portfolio/easyflix/library.jpg')"><img src="/portfolio/easyflix/library.jpg" alt="EasyFlix library screen" width="2047" height="1151" loading="eager" decoding="async" /><figcaption class="mono"><span>REAL PRODUCT CAPTURE</span><b>USER-SUPPLIED / 2047×1151</b></figcaption></figure></div>
          </a>
          <a class="project-carousel-slide" href="/projects/revdev/" data-slide aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="carousel-slide-copy"><div class="project-top"><span class="eyebrow">03 · Developer infrastructure</span><span class="project-state active">ACTIVE DEVELOPMENT</span></div><h2>RevDev</h2><p>A native Windows control surface for durable multi-project AI-assisted development, guarded execution and persistent project continuity.</p><span class="carousel-link">Open case study ↗</span></div>
            <div class="carousel-visual-column"><div class="carousel-visual carousel-console revdev-visual" aria-hidden="true"><div class="revdev-icon-stage revdev-mark-pending" aria-label="RevDev icon awaiting approved canonical asset"></div><div class="revdev-track"><span>QUEUE</span><i></i><b>READY</b></div><div class="revdev-track"><span>MISSION</span><i></i><b>GUARDED</b></div><div class="revdev-track"><span>RESULT</span><i></i><b>PERSISTED</b></div></div></div>
          </a>
          <a class="project-carousel-slide" href="/projects/reseller-ai/" data-slide aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="carousel-slide-copy"><div class="project-top"><span class="eyebrow">04 · Computer vision / resale</span><span class="project-state">FIELD TESTED</span></div><h2>Retro Game Vision &amp; Resale System</h2><p>Computer-vision-assisted field tooling for identifying, pricing and deciding what to do with retro-game inventory.</p><span class="carousel-link">Open case study ↗</span></div>
            <div class="carousel-visual-column"><div class="carousel-visual carousel-console" aria-hidden="true"><div class="priority-visual-head mono"><span>FIELD / DECISION PIPELINE</span><b>NO GUI RELEASE</b></div><div class="resale-mini-row"><span>INPUT</span><b>STORE PHOTO</b></div><div class="resale-mini-row"><span>EVIDENCE</span><b>VISION + MARKET</b></div><div class="resale-mini-row"><span>OUTPUT</span><b>BUY / RESEARCH / SKIP</b></div></div></div>
          </a>
          <div class="project-carousel-slide carousel-small-projects-slide" data-slide aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="carousel-small-header"><div><div class="project-top"><span class="eyebrow">05 · Focused tools</span><span class="project-state">SMALLER, FINISHED, INTENTIONAL</span></div><h2>Smaller but Useful</h2><p>Four compact projects, presented together so the carousel stays focused while each project remains one click away.</p></div><span class="carousel-link">Explore the focused projects ↓</span></div>
            <div class="carousel-small-grid" aria-label="Smaller but Useful projects">
              <a class="carousel-small-card" href="/projects/rainmeter-clock/" tabindex="-1"><span class="eyebrow">Desktop utility</span><h3>MinimalClock</h3><p>Compact desktop clock and Rainmeter experiment.</p><span class="carousel-small-meta mono">SHIPPED · 1.0.0 ↗</span></a>
              <a class="carousel-small-card" href="/projects/exactartifact/" tabindex="-1"><span class="eyebrow">Artifact integrity</span><h3>ExactArtifact</h3><p>Deterministic SHA-256 and manifest verification.</p><span class="carousel-small-meta mono">RELEASED · 1.0.0 ↗</span></a>
              <a class="carousel-small-card" href="/projects/gaptrace/" tabindex="-1"><span class="eyebrow">Network diagnostics</span><h3>GapTrace</h3><p>DNS, TCP and HTTP micro-outage evidence recorder.</p><span class="carousel-small-meta mono">RELEASED · 1.0.0 ↗</span></a>
              <a class="carousel-small-card" href="/projects/configtrace/" tabindex="-1"><span class="eyebrow">Configuration evidence</span><h3>ConfigTrace</h3><p>Deterministic snapshots and semantic configuration diffs.</p><span class="carousel-small-meta mono">RELEASED · 1.0.1 ↗</span></a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <span class="carousel-live mono" data-carousel-live aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></span>
        <div class="project-carousel-controls">
          <div class="carousel-controls-inner">
            <button class="carousel-rotation-toggle" type="button" data-carousel-toggle aria-label="Stop automatic slide rotation">PAUSE</button><button class="carousel-arrow" type="button" data-carousel-prev aria-label="Previous featured project">←</button>
            <div class="carousel-dots" role="group" aria-label="Featured project slides">
              <button class="carousel-dot is-active" type="button" aria-pressed="true" aria-label="Show CrashScope" data-carousel-dot="0"></button><button class="carousel-dot" type="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Show EasyFlix" data-carousel-dot="1"></button><button class="carousel-dot" type="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Show RevDev" data-carousel-dot="2"></button><button class="carousel-dot" type="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Show Retro Game Vision & Resale System" data-carousel-dot="3"></button><button class="carousel-dot" type="button" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Show Smaller but Useful" data-carousel-dot="4"></button>
            </div>
            <button class="carousel-arrow" type="button" data-carousel-next aria-label="Next featured project">→</button>
          </div>
          <span class="carousel-timer mono" aria-hidden="true"><i data-carousel-progress></i></span>
        </div>
      </section>
      </div>
    <div class="identity-proof" aria-label="Professional snapshot">
      <div><strong>1.0</strong><span>VektorDeck source available</span></div>
      <div><strong>1.3</strong><span>CrashScope current development line</span></div><div><strong>266/266</strong><span>CrashScope 1.2 automated .NET tests</span></div>
      <div><strong>219</strong><span>EasyFlix 1.4 automated tests</span></div>
      <div><strong>4,000+</strong><span>hands-on electrical trade hours</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-meta identity-skills" aria-label="Core technologies">
      <span class="pill">Python</span><span class="pill">C# / .NET</span><span class="pill">FastAPI</span><span class="pill">React</span><span class="pill">TypeScript</span><span class="pill">SQLite</span><span class="pill">Computer Vision</span><span class="pill">Windows Diagnostics</span><span class="pill">Automation</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap" id="work">
    <div class="section-head"><p class="eyebrow">Selected work</p><div><h2>Built from real use cases.</h2><p class="section-intro">Shipped systems, active engineering work and smaller focused tools are separated clearly so the state of each project is obvious.</p></div></div>

    <div class="project-tier project-tier-primary">
      <div class="project-tier-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">Core products</p><h3>Three systems worth opening first.</h3></div><p>CrashScope, EasyFlix and RevDev are the strongest expression of the portfolio's current engineering work, so they get the clearest visual treatment and the most direct path into their case studies.</p></div>

      <div class="active-project-grid">
        <a class="project compact-project priority-project crashscope-project" href="/projects/crashscope/">
          <div class="project-top"><span class="eyebrow">03 · Windows diagnostics</span><span class="project-state active">1.3 IN DEVELOPMENT · 1.2 RELEASED</span></div>
          <h3>CrashScope</h3>
          <p>A privacy-first Windows crash-diagnostics system with a native WPF/WebView2 desktop shell that correlates hardware telemetry with Event Log, WER and persistent incident evidence without pretending correlation proves root cause.</p>
          <span class="status-note">Built after repeated game, GPU and workload failures made it obvious how fragmented useful Windows diagnostic evidence can be.</span>
          <div class="priority-visual crashscope-visual" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="priority-visual-head mono"><span>CURRENT / 1.3 DEVELOPMENT</span><b>BUILD STATE</b></div>
            <div class="diagnostic-wave"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
            <div class="diagnostic-readout mono"><span>EVENT LOG</span><b>LINKED</b><span>WER</span><b>LINKED</b><span>CONFIGTRACE</span><b>OPTIONAL</b></div>
            <div class="diagnostic-foot mono"><span>266/266 TESTS</span><span>LOCAL-FIRST</span><span>ROOT CAUSE: NOT ASSUMED</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="active-build-visual">
            <div><span>1.1 AGENT CPU · AVG</span><b>0.2365%</b></div>
            <div><span>WORKING SET · AVG</span><b>91.71 MB</b></div>
            <div><span>AUTOMATED TESTS</span><b>266/266</b></div>
            <div><span>RELEASE STATE</span><b class="good">PUBLIC · 1.2.0</b></div>
          </div>
          <span class="status-note">CrashScope 1.3 is the current development line; CrashScope 1.2.0 remains the public release with a native Windows desktop shell and 266/266 automated tests. Primary AMD validation and genuine second-PC validation on Windows 10 / Intel Core i5-3210M / Intel HD Graphics 4000 both passed; NVIDIA real-hardware validation remains outstanding.</span>
          <span class="text-link">Open validated case study ↗</span>
        </a>

        <a class="project compact-project priority-project easyflix-project" href="/projects/easyflix/">
          <div class="project-top"><span class="eyebrow">04 · Windows local media</span><span class="project-state active">1.4.0 RELEASED</span></div>
          <h3>EasyFlix</h3>
          <p>A polished local-first Windows media library for legally acquired movies, TV and anime, with multi-drive discovery, watch-state continuity, metadata and subtitle workflows, and a streaming-style WPF interface.</p>
          <span class="status-note">Built around a simple constraint from my own media library: make what is already on disk feel great without rearranging or risking the source files.</span>
          <figure class="priority-screenshot easyflix-product-shot">
            <img src={baseURL + 'easyflix/home.jpg'} alt="EasyFlix home screen showing a real local media library" width="2047" height="1151" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            <div class="easyflix-shot-overlay mono" aria-hidden="true"><span>LOCAL LIBRARY</span><div><b>FILESYSTEM</b><i></i><b>WATCH STATE</b><i></i><b>PLAYBACK</b></div></div>
            <figcaption class="mono"><span>REAL PRODUCT CAPTURE</span><b>FULL-RES / HOME</b></figcaption>
          </figure>
          <div class="active-build-visual">
            <div><span>STACK</span><b>WPF · .NET 10 · SQLite</b></div>
            <div><span>MODEL</span><b>LOCAL-FIRST</b></div>
            <div><span>VALIDATION</span><b>219 TESTS · 0 WARNINGS</b></div>
            <div><span>ARTIFACT</span><b class="good">INSTALLER + PORTABLE WIN-X64</b></div>
          </div>
          <span class="status-note">1.4.0 publicly released · privacy sanitization complete · MIT public release verified</span>
          <span class="text-link">Open EasyFlix case study ↗</span>
        </a>

        <a class="project compact-project priority-project revdev-project" href="/projects/revdev/">
          <div class="project-top"><span class="eyebrow">Developer infrastructure</span><span class="project-state active">ACTIVE DEVELOPMENT</span></div>
          <h3>RevDev</h3>
          <p>A native Windows control surface for durable multi-project AI-assisted development via Dev Relay, with guarded execution, deterministic project state, a five-tool hub, failure learning and local-first validation.</p>
          <span class="status-note">Built to keep long-running AI-assisted engineering work visible and resumable across projects, chats and model boundaries without handing execution authority to the UI.</span>
          <div class="priority-visual revdev-visual" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="priority-visual-head mono"><span>REVDEV / OPERATOR</span><b>BUILDING</b></div>
            <div class="revdev-track"><span>QUEUE</span><i></i><b>READY</b></div>
            <div class="revdev-track"><span>MISSION</span><i></i><b>GUARDED</b></div>
            <div class="revdev-track"><span>RESULT</span><i></i><b>PERSISTED</b></div>
            <div class="diagnostic-foot mono"><span>GIT</span><span>RESULTS</span><span>GOALS</span><span>HOSTED_DENY</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="active-build-visual">
            <div><span>STACK</span><b>.NET 8 · WPF</b></div>
            <div><span>TOOLS</span><b>5 PROVIDERS</b></div>
            <div><span>CONTINUITY</span><b>GIT · RESULTS · GOALS</b></div>
            <div><span>SAFETY</span><b class="good">LOCAL-FIRST · HOSTED_DENY</b></div>
          </div>
          <span class="status-note">Active development is focused on restart-safe state, grouped multi-step progress and liveness, and final release-lifecycle hardening before any public release.</span>
          <span class="text-link">Open active case study ↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>



    <div class="project-tier">
      <div class="project-tier-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">Flagship systems</p><h3>Built, validated and field-tested.</h3></div><p>The deepest case studies: products with substantial architecture, validation and real-world use behind them.</p></div>

      <div class="featured-project">
        <a class="project project-featured" href="/projects/reseller-ai/">
          <div class="project-copy">
            <div class="project-kicker"><span class="eyebrow">01 · Flagship system</span><span class="project-state">FIELD TESTED</span></div>
            <h3>Retro Game Vision &<br />Resale System</h3>
            <p>A pipeline that turns Japanese second-hand store photos into traceable resale decisions while preserving uncertainty, evidence lineage and exact physical-copy state.</p>
            <span class="status-note">Started after noticing that a cheap price tag in a Japanese retro shop was rarely enough evidence to know whether a copy was actually worth buying.</span>
            <div class="project-tags"><span>Python</span><span>SQLite</span><span>Vision</span><span>Decision systems</span><span>CI</span></div>
            <span class="text-link">Open case study ↗</span>
          </div>
          <div class="resale-visual" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="visual-head mono"><span>DECISION ENGINE</span><span>LIVE MODEL</span></div>
            <div class="decision-item"><span class="decision-index">A-042</span><div><strong>Japanese PS1 title</strong><small>compatible evidence · 4 observations</small></div><b class="buy">BUY</b></div>
            <div class="decision-item"><span class="decision-index">A-043</span><div><strong>Collector edition</strong><small>edition mismatch detected</small></div><b class="research">RESEARCH</b></div>
            <div class="decision-item"><span class="decision-index">A-044</span><div><strong>Disc-only copy</strong><small>condition adjusted · margin below gate</small></div><b class="skip">SKIP</b></div>
            <div class="integrity mono"><span>FOREIGN KEYS: 0</span><span>INTEGRITY: OK</span><span>EVIDENCE: LINKED</span></div>
          </div>
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="project-grid secondary-grid">
        <a class="project compact-project project-showcase" href="/projects/vektordeck/">
          <div class="project-showcase-copy">
            <div class="project-top"><span class="eyebrow">02 · Flagship system</span><span class="project-state">1.0.0</span></div>
            <h3>VektorDeck</h3>
            <p>A local-first AI workstation manager for GGUF model intelligence, safe runtime ownership, hardware telemetry, evidence-aware benchmarking and explainable launch recommendations.</p>
            <span class="status-note">Built because my own local-AI setup had become too dependent on exact flags, scattered model files and terminal archaeology.</span>
            <div class="forge-visual mono" aria-hidden="true">
              <div><span>QWEN 27B · IQ3_XS</span><b>11.15 GB</b></div><div class="meter"><i style="width:82%"></i></div>
              <div><span>SMART LAUNCH</span><b>8K · EXPERIMENTAL</b></div><div class="meter"><i style="width:64%"></i></div>
              <div><span>RELEASE READINESS</span><b>0 BLOCKERS</b></div>
            </div>
            <span class="text-link">Open 1.0 case study ↗</span>
          </div>
          <figure class="project-snapshot">
            <img src={`${baseURL}vektordeck/dashboard.webp`} alt="VektorDeck 1.0 dashboard with hardware telemetry and local runtime controls" width="1920" height="1079" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            <figcaption class="mono"><span>REAL PRODUCT / 1.0</span><b>LOCAL WORKSTATION · SOURCE AVAILABLE</b></figcaption>
          </figure>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="project-tier">
      <div class="project-tier-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">Focused projects</p><h3>Small, finished, intentional.</h3></div><p>Compact projects that show interface craft or a focused technical idea without pretending to be flagship systems.</p></div>
      <div class="focused-project-grid" aria-label="Focused projects">
        <a class="project compact-project clock-project" href="/projects/rainmeter-clock/">
          <div class="project-top"><span class="eyebrow">05 · Desktop experiment</span><span class="project-state">SHIPPED</span></div>
          <h3>MinimalClock</h3>
          <p>A compact desktop clock experiment in browser rendering, typography and lightweight Rainmeter integration.</p>
          <span class="status-note">A tiny utility I wanted on my own desktop became an exercise in measuring overhead, packaging cleanly and resisting unnecessary runtime complexity.</span>
          <div class="clock-visual mono" aria-hidden="true"><strong id="portfolio-clock">20:25</strong><span>LOCAL / SYSTEM TIME</span></div>
          <span class="text-link">View focused project ↗</span>
        </a>
        <a class="project compact-project" href="/projects/exactartifact/">
          <div class="project-top"><span class="eyebrow">06 · Artifact integrity</span><span class="project-state">1.0.0</span></div>
          <h3>ExactArtifact</h3>
          <p>A compact C#/.NET integrity utility for streaming SHA-256, deterministic directory manifests and precise mismatch reporting, with both CLI and WPF interfaces.</p>
          <span class="status-note">Built to make “is this exactly the artifact I tested?” answerable with deterministic evidence rather than filenames or assumptions.</span>
          <div class="active-build-visual" aria-hidden="true">
            <div><span>STACK</span><b>C# · .NET · WPF</b></div>
            <div><span>AUTOMATED TESTS</span><b>22 PASS</b></div>
            <div><span>HASHING</span><b>STREAMING SHA-256</b></div>
            <div><span>RELEASE</span><b class="good">1.0.0</b></div>
          </div>
          <span class="text-link">Open focused project ↗</span>
        </a>

        <a class="project compact-project" href="/projects/gaptrace/">
          <div class="project-top"><span class="eyebrow">07 · Network diagnostics</span><span class="project-state">1.0.0</span></div>
          <h3>GapTrace</h3>
          <p>A lightweight Go utility that records DNS, TCP and HTTP reachability, classifies micro-outages, preserves CSV evidence and analyzes recovery windows.</p>
          <span class="status-note">Built after intermittent mobile-tether failures were too brief and inconsistent for ordinary “is the internet working?” tests to explain.</span>
          <div class="active-build-visual" aria-hidden="true">
            <div><span>STACK</span><b>GO · CONCURRENCY</b></div>
            <div><span>PEAK WORKING SET</span><b>16.2 MB</b></div>
            <div><span>CPU · VALIDATION RUN</span><b>0.016 s</b></div>
            <div><span>RELEASE</span><b class="good">1.0.0</b></div>
          </div>
          <span class="text-link">Open focused project ↗</span>
        </a>

        <a class="project compact-project" href="/projects/configtrace/">
          <div class="project-top"><span class="eyebrow">08 · Configuration evidence</span><span class="project-state">1.0.1</span></div>
          <h3>ConfigTrace</h3>
          <p>A Rust configuration-change tracer with deterministic snapshots, semantic field diffs, privacy-aware redaction and an event-driven JSONL journal.</p>
          <span class="status-note">Built as a standalone low-overhead evidence provider that can also integrate cleanly with CrashScope without binding CrashScope to Rust internals.</span>
          <div class="active-build-visual" aria-hidden="true">
            <div><span>STACK</span><b>RUST · JSONL</b></div>
            <div><span>IDLE PEAK WORKING SET</span><b>4.3 MB</b></div>
            <div><span>IDLE CPU · 10 S</span><b>0.016 s</b></div>
            <div><span>RELEASE</span><b class="good">1.0.1</b></div>
          </div>
          <span class="text-link">Open focused project ↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="home-about-strip">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">About Marcelo</p><h3>Technical work, people skills, and a hands-on engineering path.</h3></div>
      <div><p>I came into software through years of electrical work and international customer-facing roles, then started building the tools I wished existed. That background is why the projects here care so much about real constraints, failure modes, evidence and maintainability.</p><a class="button" href="/about/">Read the professional profile ↗</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="home-about-strip" aria-label="Recruiter contact">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Open to work</p><h3>Software engineering, QA / automation and technical systems roles.</h3></div>
      <div>
        <p>I am looking for remote-friendly teams where practical debugging, software reliability, clear communication and the ability to learn quickly matter. The case studies above show the work; these links make the next step easy.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button primary" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/marcelo-ellwanger-10657a435/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">LinkedIn ↗</a>
          <a class="button" href="https://github.com/marcelosofficial-ctrl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub ↗</a>
          <a class="button" href="/contact/">Contact ↗</a>
          <a class="button" href="/resume/software/">Software / QA Résumé ↗</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="field-note wrap" aria-label="Personal field note">
    <div class="field-note-mark mono">FIELD NOTE / 001</div>
    <blockquote>Most of these projects began the same way: I got curious, then annoyed that the tool I wanted didn’t exist.</blockquote>
    <div class="field-note-signoff"><span class="note-line"></span><span>Marcelo</span></div>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap principles" id="about">
    <div class="section-head"><p class="eyebrow">How I work</p><div><h2>Build. Test. Find the edge case. Rebuild.</h2></div></div>
    <div class="principle-grid">
      <article><span class="mono principle-no">01</span><h3>Start with reality.</h3><p>I prefer problems with imperfect inputs, awkward constraints and a reason for the software to exist beyond the demo.</p></article>
      <article><span class="mono principle-no">02</span><h3>Keep the evidence.</h3><p>I care about provenance, explicit uncertainty and systems that can explain why they produced a result.</p></article>
      <article><span class="mono principle-no">03</span><h3>Make failure useful.</h3><p>Unexpected cases become tests, architecture decisions and better boundaries rather than something to hide from the portfolio.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script is:inline>
    const clock = document.getElementById('portfolio-clock');
    const tick = () => {
      if (!clock) return;
      clock.textContent = new Intl.DateTimeFormat([], { hour: '2-digit', minute: '2-digit', hour12: false }).format(new Date());
    };
    tick();
    setInterval(tick, 1000);
  </script>



</BaseLayout>
